Input: {"question": "Who is the main character in \"The Lost Prince\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d00", "start": 0, "end": 135, "text": "The Lost Prince (Burnett novel) The Lost Prince is a novel by British-American author Frances Hodgson Burnett, first published in 1915."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d00", "start": 136, "end": 232, "text": "This book is about Marco Loristan, his father, and his friend, a street urchin called \"The Rat\"."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d00", "start": 233, "end": 349, "text": "Marco's father, Stefan, is a Samavian patriot working to overthrow the cruel dictatorship in the kingdom of Samavia."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d00", "start": 350, "end": 469, "text": "Marco and his father come to London where Marco strikes up a friendship with a crippled street urchin known as The Rat."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d00", "start": 470, "end": 547, "text": "The friendship occurs when Marco overhears The Rat shouting in military form."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d00", "start": 548, "end": 600, "text": "Marco discovers he had stumbled upon a club known as"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 0, "end": 1, "text": "."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 2, "end": 68, "text": "Marco knew it was because he was startled to find them only boys ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 69, "end": 122, "text": "He made a step forward to look at them more closely ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 123, "end": 147, "text": "`` The Lamp is lighted !"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 148, "end": 175, "text": "And you two bear the Sign !"}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 176, "end": 193, "text": "'' he exclaimed ."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 194, "end": 255, "text": "Marco stood out in the fire glow that he might see him well ."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 256, "end": 281, "text": "He saluted with respect ."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 282, "end": 336, "text": "`` My name is Marco Loristan , Highness , '' he said ."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 337, "end": 363, "text": "`` And my father sent me ."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 364, "end": 440, "text": "'' The change which came upon his face then was even greater than at first ."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d01", "start": 441, "end": 444, "text": "For"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "on a throne wearing a crown ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 30, "end": 79, "text": "I wonder if it would make a chap look different ?"}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 80, "end": 207, "text": "” He laughed his squeaky laugh , and then turned in his sudden way to Marco : “ But he ’ d be a fool to give up the vengeance ."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 208, "end": 227, "text": "What is your name ?"}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 228, "end": 248, "text": "” “ Marco Loristan ."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 249, "end": 265, "text": "What ’ s yours ?"}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 266, "end": 292, "text": "It isn ’ t The Rat really."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 293, "end": 319, "text": "” “ It ’ s Jem RATcliffe ."}, "D3S9": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 320, "end": 342, "text": "That ’ s pretty near ."}, "D3S10": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 343, "end": 362, "text": "Where do you live ?"}, "D3S11": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 363, "end": 371, "text": "” “ No ."}, "D3S12": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 372, "end": 390, "text": "7 Philibert Place."}, "D3S13": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d02", "start": 391, "end": 399, "text": "” “ This"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 0, "end": 13, "text": "`` Excuse me?"}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 14, "end": 68, "text": "'' The gentleman's clever eyes scrutinized him keenly."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 69, "end": 99, "text": "Then he also spoke in English."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 100, "end": 133, "text": "`` Perhaps you do not understand?"}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 134, "end": 208, "text": "I asked your name because you are very like a Samavian I know, '' he said."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 209, "end": 254, "text": "`` I am Prince Ivan, '' the boy answered him."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 255, "end": 304, "text": "The man looked straight into his eyes and smiled."}, "D4S8": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 305, "end": 340, "text": "`` That is not the name,'' he said."}, "D4S9": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 341, "end": 370, "text": "`` I beg your pardon, my boy."}, "D4S10": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d03", "start": 371, "end": 412, "text": "'' He was about to go on, and had indeed."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d04", "start": 0, "end": 314, "text": "9.99 $ 9.99 - $ 9.99 Current price $ 9.99 | / Choose a variant Paperback - $ 9.99 Binding Paperback Quantity Add to cart About The Rightful King The story of twelve-year-old The Rat, the crippled street urchin who becomes the key figure in the mission to overthrow the cruel dictatorship in the kingdom of Samavia."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d04", "start": 315, "end": 409, "text": "The Rat befriends Marco Loristan, whose father Stefan is working to restore the rightful king."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d04", "start": 410, "end": 492, "text": "Stefan entrusts the two boys on a secret mission across Europe with a secret sign."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d04", "start": 493, "end": 591, "text": "The two young boys begin an adventure of a lifetime and along the way discover their true destiny."}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d05", "start": 0, "end": 138, "text": "The Lost Prince (Edwards novel) The Lost Prince is a sequel to the best-selling novel \"The Little Book\" by American writer Selden Edwards."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d05", "start": 139, "end": 181, "text": "It was published by Dutton in August 2012."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d05", "start": 182, "end": 386, "text": "\"The Lost Prince\" follows the character of Eleanor Burden, an 1890s Boston socialite who has resigned herself to marrying the man she should be with rather than the man she wants, whom she lost in Vienna."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d05", "start": 387, "end": 572, "text": "What separates her from others of her station and background is that Eleanor believes that she has the ability to predict all of the major historical events that will occur while she is"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d06", "start": 0, "end": 34, "text": "( admittedly high ) expectations ."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d06", "start": 35, "end": 260, "text": "The Lost Prince is a companion to The Little Book ; whereas that was the story of Wheeler Burden in fin de siecle Vienna , this is the story of Eleanor Burden after her return from Vienna , up through the end of World War I ."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d06", "start": 261, "end": 376, "text": "The Little Book was a compelling tale , and it provides the background necessary to make sense of The Lost Prince ."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d06", "start": 377, "end": 502, "text": "I honestly do not know how this will read for people who have n't read The Little Book ; it may prove confusing or disjointed"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d07", "start": 0, "end": 295, "text": "Ebook Aug 16 , 2012 | ISBN 9781101590973 Buy from Other Retailers : Buy the Ebook : Kobo Barnes & Noble Apple Books A Million Amazon Google Play Store About The Lost Prince “ The Lost Prince can stand independently of The Little Book … but why deprive yourself of the pleasures of reading both ?"}, "D8S2": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d07", "start": 296, "end": 533, "text": "” — Booklist Recently returned from fin de siècle Vienna , where she tragically lost the first great love of her life , Eleanor Burden settles into her expected place in Boston society , marries a suitable husband , and waits for life to"}, "D9S1": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d08", "start": 0, "end": 114, "text": "a glimpse of an approaching comet, Johnnie's parents are called to Buckingham Palace to be by the King's deathbed."}, "D9S2": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d08", "start": 115, "end": 254, "text": "During the funeral attended by all the heads of state of Europe, including the Kaiser Wilhelm, Johnnie succumbs to a serious epileptic fit."}, "D9S3": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d08", "start": 255, "end": 373, "text": "Queen Mary, Johnnie's mother, summons doctors to examine him and their diagnosis confirms her and Lalla's worst fears."}, "D9S4": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d08", "start": 374, "end": 457, "text": "Lalla volunteers to look after Johnnie to prevent him being sent to an institution."}, "D9S5": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d08", "start": 458, "end": 602, "text": "The two of them are to be sent to Sandringham, where Johnnie is to be prevented from encountering anybody but the closest members of his family."}, "D10S1": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d09", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "of Archduke Franz Ferdinand ."}, "D10S2": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d09", "start": 30, "end": 95, "text": "Realising this has been withheld from him , the King is furious ."}, "D10S3": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d09", "start": 96, "end": 202, "text": "Unnoticed by the adults , Johnnie pursues Charlotte , as the terrified bird flies away into the building ."}, "D10S4": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d09", "start": 203, "end": 340, "text": "The Queen , Lalla and George go searching for Johnnie and his mother is shocked when she sees one of Johnnie 's fits for the first time ."}, "D10S5": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d09", "start": 341, "end": 442, "text": "As officials gather for diplomatic meetings , Johnnie is taken back to the isolation of Sandringham ."}, "D10S6": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d09", "start": 443, "end": 554, "text": "Episode Two Prince George witnesses the brinkmanship between the Allies and the Central Powers , led by Germany"}, "D11S1": {"document_number": 11, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d10", "start": 0, "end": 635, "text": "5.2 Sales 5.3 Awards and nominations 6 Notes 7 References 8 External links Toggle the table of contents Prince of Persia : The Lost Crown 14 languages العربية Español فارسی Français Bahasa Indonesia Italiano עברית Ladin Bahasa Melayu Nederlands Português Русский Suomi 中文 Edit links Article Talk English Read Edit View history Tools Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide"}, "D12S1": {"document_number": 12, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0381-225925a9d2bf:d11", "start": 0, "end": 417, "text": "2017 ) HNR Issue 78 ( November 2016 ) HNR Issue 77 ( August 2016 ) HNR Issue 76 ( May 2016 ) HNR Issue 75 ( February 2016 ) HNR Issue 74 ( November 2015 ) HNR Issue 73 ( August 2015 ) HNR Issue 72 ( May 2015 ) HNR Issue 71 ( February 2015 ) HNR Issue 70 ( November 2014 ) HNR Issue 69 ( August 2014 ) HNR Issue 68 ( May 2014 ) HNR Issue 67 ( February 2014 ) HNR Issue 66 ( November 2013 ) HNR Issue 65 ( August 2013 )"}}, "original_cards": [{"do